WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
I'm in Hull, a small seaside town near Boston
in the northeast United States.

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.680
I grew up visiting the British equivalent
of towns like this, and sure,

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:08.820
it's the middle of winter,

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.870
it is so bitterly cold here
that the ocean foam has frozen.

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:14.300
There aren't any tourists, nearly everything's
closed for the season,

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:18.250
but this town still feels a little like home to me.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:21.280
There is one place on the seafront here
that's open specially today though.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.600
And it's the last play-for-cash
Fascination Parlor in the world.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.350
- A lot of these did
exist back in the day.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:32.790
I'm not exactly sure how many, all I do
know is: this is the longest standing.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:35.840
A hundred years old last year.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.720
It was transported up here sometime over
the past century from Coney Island

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.250
and now sits here on Nantasket Beach.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:43.810
There are 64 machines here,

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.420
so on a busy night here we'll
have 64 players.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:49.580
The game begins with
your bill on the glass,

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:51.260
we'll range anywhere from a quarter

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:54.330
to a dollar and maybe two
dollars at a point in time.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:56.560
We have the entertainment
and gaming licence

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:59.680
for anyone to come in and play,
as long as you're over 18 years old.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.420
It is a game of skill.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.680
Like everything in life, there is some luck that goes into it,

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:07.600
but certainly there are some skilled players
that I have witnessed over the past year.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.470
- So here are the rules:
roll the balls into the holes.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.600
Each time you sink a ball,

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.040
the corresponding light
on the board switches on.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.040
First to get a line of five,
horizontal, vertical or diagonal, wins,

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.970
or in some cases, first to
light up the whole board.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:21.960
And here, you win cash.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.340
There are other Fascination parlors

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:25.140
but this is the only one
where you're not playing

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.880
for tokens you can
redeem, you're not playing

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:30.290
against the house, you are
playing against everyone else.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.860
And if win, you're taking their money.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:35.140
With the house taking a cut, of course.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:37.820
But it is winter, it's the off-season,
there are no tourists,

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:41.070
so today I am just playing
against Chas, the owner.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:42.560
Do you have three balls there?

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:44.440
- I do, I'm ready to go,
how 'bout yourself?

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:45.800
- Alright, so it's a dollar?

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:46.633
- Dollar on the glass.

00:01:46.633 --> 00:01:47.980
Where's my dollar bill?

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:49.749
Think I might be out,
but let me double check.

00:01:49.749 --> 00:01:51.769
- Do you need to borrow a dollar(?)
- I think I do.

00:01:51.769 --> 00:01:53.020
[laughs]

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:53.853
Thank you sir.

00:01:53.853 --> 00:01:56.710
- Alright dollar on the glass.
- Dollar on the glass.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:58.010
- Alright, good luck Tom.
- Alright.

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:00.239
- Three, two, one, roll 'em.

00:02:00.239 --> 00:02:02.180
[balls rattling]

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:03.500
- So, we're playing to cover here.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:04.810
- Playing to cover.
- Okay.

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:06.520
- [CHAS] "It is winter right now,

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.100
"so the plan for the next few months
is to reestablish the arcade,

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.800
"shake it up a little bit in there,

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.880
"meaning we're looking to make it easy

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:16.240
"for everyone to join,
understand the rules,

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:18.130
"and get in here and be a part of the fun."

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:19.390
- How do you aim?

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:22.740
- [CHAS] "Every so often, these
games will peter out because of their age,

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:23.880
"and there's a local gentleman

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:26.510
"who comes in on a weekend,
fixes them for us,

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:28.050
"so we get right back at it the next week.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:30.230
""It is still running on
century-old technology,

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:32.920
"just a few different components
are changed in and out, of course.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.840
"They are all tied together into one circuit
and work amongst themselves."

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.960
- Am I in the lead?
I think I'm in the lead, just.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:42.293
- Oh yeah, it's by three or four there!
I gotta catch up.

00:02:42.293 --> 00:02:45.600
[CHAS] "I think there's a place
for it to expand and grow

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.244
"and be in a lot of different
places throughout the world

00:02:48.244 --> 00:02:51.670
"but the reason it isn't
everywhere is, I think,

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:54.780
"we are a part of the technological era,

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:58.120
"and with different ways
that you can stay busy nowadays,

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:02.360
"cell phones and gaming consoles,
televisions,

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:06.695
"there are other things that pull away
from old-fashioned fun, if you will."

00:03:06.695 --> 00:03:10.100
- It's just not... yes, okay, three!
I've got three, you've got four.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.790
[CHAS] - "We're going to continue to build
off of the history that Fascination,

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:15.350
"here on Nantasket Beach,
has had for decades.

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:18.130
"I've heard numerous stories of the folks

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.880
"that used to run this over
the past five or six decades,

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.730
"even more, and I wish
these walls could talk

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:24.923
"because there would be
a lot to talk about."

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:28.690
- Oh, come on, I've got one.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:30.900
[TOM] "What I love about this is that these are

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.880
"century-old machines,
built with the same relays

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:37.220
"that powered old telephone exchanges,
and they're all interlocked together,

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:40.310
"in one really complicated circuit.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:45.030
"No microelectronics, no wifi, just a lot of
things that go clunk and buzz."

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:47.160
[CHAS] - "So when someone lights up the board,

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.160
"everyone on the sidewalk,
everybody in here

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.550
"can hear it and they know about it.

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:53.650
"There's usually cheering,
all the lights on the board go off

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:57.090
"and the gentleman calling the game,
or the woman calling the game,

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:01.390
"will make the announcement that
the winner is at, for example, 'table 13!'"

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:02.750
This has got to be it, come on.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:04.799
- I've hit the one next to the one I need

00:04:04.799 --> 00:04:06.529
six times now.
- Game over, Tom!

00:04:06.529 --> 00:04:08.363
[bell ringing]
Winner, winner!

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:12.130
Good game sir, I'll take
that and I'll take that.

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:14.046
- Yep, so close.

00:04:14.046 --> 00:04:15.453
[bell ringing, then stops]

00:04:15.453 --> 00:04:18.020
That was genuinely fun.
- That was, isn't it?

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:19.670
The cool thing is, you get these folks

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:21.850
who have never played
before, they sit down,

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:23.870
have just as much fun as we just had

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:25.790
and whether they've played
it once or twice before,

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:26.623
next thing you know they're here

00:04:26.623 --> 00:04:28.380
for three hours long, and as you can see,

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:30.790
it seems easier than it actually is.

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.740
- Yeah, cause the first one's like,
oh, I'm lighting everything up,

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:35.194
and then, you cannot nail the one.

00:04:35.194 --> 00:04:36.940
- Yeah, you cannot, you look and you try

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:39.520
probably twelve times.
- Yeah. [laughs]

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:41.650
Thank you.
- Yes sir, thank you Tom.

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:44.340
- Thank you to Chas and all the team here
at the Paragon Boardwalk.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:45.470
You can pull down the description

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:47.853
for more about them and
about the Fascination Parlor.

